Aggregate information is also used to help us run and maintain our site, study traffic patterns and generally learn about the usage of our site. Some of this aggregate information may be used to help us set advertising rates, determine advertising fees, and attract advertisers and co-branding partners.
An IP address is a number assigned to your computer when you connect to the Internet. As part of the protocol of the Internet, web servers can identify your computer by its IP address. In addition, web servers may be able to identify the type of browser you are using or even the type of computer.
CommunityCalendars.net sites collect IP addresses and related information for the purposes of system administration, to assess the traffic to our site, to report aggregate information to our advertisers, and to maintain and improve our site. We do[ not] link IP addresses to your personally identifiable information. We can and will use IP[ addresses],[ however], to identify a user when we feel it is[ necessary] to enforce compliance with our terms of service or to protect our service, site, customers or others.
Information provided to[ us] will[ not be shared] with[ or disclosed] by[ us] to any third party unless you have granted your permission[ for such] use[.] Users[ who] include their web site in their signatures in various parts of this site, or who provide us with their email address[ voluntarily] as part of their event description form will have[ only] their web site and email address[ disclosed.] Any personally identifiable information placed on any site linked to this site is[ placed] at the discretion of the user, and is[ not bound by] this policy.
Certain federal, state, and local regulations may[ require] that[ we disclose non-]public personal information about[ you.] In those circumstances,[ only the specific information] requested by subpoena[ or] court order[ will be provided] to the requesting[ party, and only for their use.]
